Z||000000||danny boy||03-08-2001||12:28 AM||||   Took the GT to my friends house tonight to bleed the brakes. I just put the G/A calipers/rotors on the back.After we got them bled, we decided to go for a test drive. He hasn't been behind the wheel of a Fiero for a LONG time,and this was the first time I had since I brought it back from Alabama. He drives VWs and I'm used to my Japanese Sport/luxury Monster so driving a Fiero hard was interesting to say the least.<BR>  I was doing about 50 going into a 35 mph turn(65mph for the Stealth) when all of a sudden we were facing the other way.Scared the bejesus out of both of us.He drove back. He wanted to see how the brakes worked in a panic stop situation.Apparently I have too much proportioning to the rear-the back locked up and we ended up sideways almost in the ditch.<BR>  That about does it for driving my fiero like it handles good...<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/stealth_feb2.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||mshill||03-08-2001||12:19 PM||||So Ogre was right. ||||reg||11
